From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robin Snyders <robin@snyders.xyz>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 15:05:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: hotdog: enable microphone routing

The SLIM Capture 1 back end already links SLIMBUS_0_TX to the WCD9340
AIF1_CAP port, and the codec node already carries micbias1 through
micbias4. No DAPM route connects an analogue microphone input to its bias
supply, so every ADC path stays powered down and the capture front end has
no reachable back end.

Add the five analogue microphone routes. The bias assignment is read from
the stock OxygenOS device tree overlay for this handset, which is
identified by carrying oplus,speaker-pa = "nxp", oplus,usbc-switch and
qcom,wsa-max-devs = <0>, and which is immediately followed by the
tfa98xx_right@34 amplifier node. Its qcom,audio-routing names the physical
role of each input:

  AMIC1 - MIC BIAS1
  AMIC2 - MIC BIAS2, "Headset Mic"
  AMIC3 - MIC BIAS4, "ANCRight Headset Mic"
  AMIC4 - MIC BIAS1, "ANCLeft Headset Mic"
  AMIC5 - MIC BIAS1, "Handset Mic"

The handset microphone is therefore AMIC5, reached by selecting AMIC5 on
the shared AMIC4_5 mux and taking ADC4. AMIC4 is an ANC input on the same
mux, which is why picking it produces a running but silent capture.

Mainline has no "Handset Mic" or "Analog Mic" input widget, so only the
pad-to-supply half of the stock routing is expressed here, as
sdm845-oneplus-fajita does for the same codec.

This change is capture-only. It adds no playback route and does not touch
the validated speaker path.

Signed-off-by: Robin Snyders <robin@snyders.xyz>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts
@@ -390,7 +390,12 @@
 	pinctrl-names = "default";
 	status = "okay";

-	audio-routing = "RX_BIAS", "MCLK";
+	audio-routing = "RX_BIAS", "MCLK",
+			"AMIC1", "MIC BIAS1",
+			"AMIC2", "MIC BIAS2",
+			"AMIC3", "MIC BIAS4",
+			"AMIC4", "MIC BIAS1",
+			"AMIC5", "MIC BIAS1";

 	mm1-dai-link {
 		link-name = "MultiMedia1";
--
2.50.1
